      "id": 96585,
      "name": "MindWanderer",
      "username": "MindWanderer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-10-18T18:31:36.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Sorry for the thread resurrection, but I had been playing it this way, then ran across this:</p><div><div><div><p><a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/103261#comment-103261\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Keywords are not Game Text, and Game Text does not include Keywords.</a></p></div></div></div><p>So the covered room is still a Room, and multiple Entry Points can stack on it. &nbsp;Unfortunately, it was also ruled that destroying the room doesn't destroy the Entry Points, so this just plain sucks for the players.</p><p>Unless there's another ruling or something I'm missing?</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:23:44.439Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
