          "clicks": 0
        }
      ],
      "read": false,
      "user_title": "",
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Sorry for the thread resurrection, but I had been playing it this way, then ran across this:</p><div class=\"field field-name-comment-body field-type-text-long field-label-hidden\" style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: &quot;Open Sans&quot;, HelveticaNeue, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><div class=\"field-items\"><div class=\"field-item even\" property=\"content:encoded\"><p style=\"margin: 0px 10px 20px 0px;\"><a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/103261#comment-103261\">Keywords are not Game Text, and Game Text does not include Keywords.</a></p></div></div></div><p>So the covered room is still a Room, and multiple Entry Points can stack on it. &nbsp;Unfortunately, it was also ruled that destroying the room doesn&#39;t destroy the Entry Points, so this just plain sucks for the players.</p><p>Unless there&#39;s another ruling or something I&#39;m missing?</p>",
